[2] Q11 -- aperiodicity: a binary word of prime length p and weight not 0 or p
    has p DISTINCT rotations.  Step 7 of the argument is exactly this.
  [PASS] Q11  0 words with non-trivial rotation stabiliser / 2208 binary words of length p in {3,5,7,11} with weight in 1..p-1; EXHAUSTIVE, exclusion list EMPTY

[3] POP-B -- f CONSTRUCTED to carry a 2-direction, at four primes and at
    non-axis directions too.  Construction: choose the labelling L with every
    u-orbit of weight t, set d_u f = a + L*s with s = -t^{-1} u, and integrate
    along the orbit (consistent because sum_i c_u = -u).  This realises EXACTLY
    the hypothesis |A_u| = 2 and nothing else, so it is a population of the
    theorem's hypothesis rather than of one A-class.

